1. Data Visualisation and Insights
It doesn’t just track whether you’ve ‘done it or not’; it also generates charts showing you:
The number of consecutive days you’ve stuck to your routine
Which days you’re most likely to miss

2. Personalised Recommendations
Based on your data, the system will suggest:
“You usually forget to drink water on Friday evenings – would you like to set a special reminder?”
“You haven’t been running for three days in a row – would you like to lower your target a little?”

3. Positive Incentives
Stay motivated through achievement badges and earning points for completing habits.

4. Smart Reminders(It’s a bit of a challenge for us; we’ll decide whether to go ahead with it later.)
These aren’t just reminders at fixed times; they’re tailored to your daily routine and progress, sending notifications at the most appropriate moments. 
For example, if you often exercise in the evenings, it will remind you after you finish work.
